<title>CHINA: Winton interim net HK$51 mln.</title>
<headline>Winton interim net HK$51 mln.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended June 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   12.1	 vs 10.1</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    4.0	  vs 3.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  17.42 loss vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    50.995     vs 42.398 (see note)</p>
<p>    Turnover		     753.58     vs 659.87 (see note)</p>
<p>    Company name		 Winton Holdings (Bermuda) Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  August 11-15</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   August 27</p>
<p>NOTE - Winton is a taxi-financing and restaurant group.</p>
<p>The company has changed its financial year end date to December 31 from March 31. Comparative figures are for six-months ended September 30, 1996.</p>
<p>The comparative figures have been restated to reflect the effect of netting off interest, which reduced the turnover to HK$659.87 million from HK$707.50 million. A change in accounting policy has also resulted in an increase of net profit to HK$42.398 million from HK$36.346 million.</p>
<p>Exceptional item is loss from sale of discontinued operations.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
